# J26 — Local monorepo baseline: whole-repository context/inventory attempt.
#
# Drives the closest thing the current product has to a holistic pass —
# `context:build` — against the real local monorepo checkout (~440k tracked
# files) and records what actually happens: duration, truncation/partial
# disclosure, revision binding, and what the Map page claims afterwards.
# A timeout here is itself baseline evidence (SCALE/RESOURCE), not a
# harness failure: the wait bound is generous and the timed-out screen is
# captured honestly.
#
# This journey writes only Kuzushi's own engagement artifacts under
# <target>/.kuzushi (the product's normal operation). It never touches
# target sources or git state, and never deletes pre-existing state.
#
# Known baseline defects this journey evidences (gap-ledger candidates):
#   - The inventory walk is a plain fs::read_dir walk hard-capped at
#     100k entries with no git-index enumeration, no persistence outside
#     the context snapshot, and no revision binding on the snapshot file.
#   - Truncation disclosure ("PARTIAL") may or may not survive to the
#     screen the operator actually reads — the expect below records which.
name: Monorepo baseline · holistic context build on real target
require-env: KUZUSHI_DEVEX_TARGET
size: 120x36
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1
launch: --target @TARGET
wait-for: 60 KUZUSHI
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
wait: 2
submit: run context:build {}
wait-for: 900 run receipt
wait: 2
snap: context-build-receipt
ask: Receipt — does the completed whole-repo build disclose partial coverage / the walk cap on this ~440k-file repository, or does it present the bounded walk as complete?
# Honest-coverage disclosure (expected to record current truth either way):
expect: PARTIAL
nav-mode:
keys: 1
wait-live-snap: 30 Viewing Map | map-after-build
expect: PROJECT CONTEXT
ask: Map — after the build, does PROJECT CONTEXT bind the snapshot to the target revision, disclose truncation, and populate the scope tree with real member names from the monorepo (not a flat or empty list)?
ask: NEXT SCANS — with no root holistic baseline accepted, does the recommendation surface stay gated, or does it already emit child-scope recommendations?
keys: Escape
